"""In-place ``aten::_foreach_log1p_`` on Ascend (Triton).

Semantics: for every tensor in the list, apply ``x <- log1p(x)`` elementwise
into the tensor's own storage, preserving data_ptr and strides.  Returns None.

Design notes
------------
* The op is element-wise and in place, so the *set* of touched addresses of a
  non-overlapping-and-dense tensor is exactly ``[ptr, ptr + numel)``.  Such a
  tensor (contiguous, transposed, permuted-dense, ...) can be walked with a flat
  linear index and needs no per-dimension arithmetic at all.
* Gappy views are collapsed to the smallest equivalent (sizes, strides) pair and
  handled by one generic rank<=8 kernel with a single tail mask.
* Math is fp32 inside the kernel for fp16/bf16 inputs (ATen float opmath) and is
  cast back to the storage dtype with round-to-nearest before the store.
* Every extra kernel launch costs ~0.09 ms of dispatch on this target, so
  tensors that share (device, dtype, numel) are served by ONE launch that takes
  up to 16 pointer arguments and walks them with a static unrolled loop.
"""

